# Cloudflare Pages reads this file from the build output directory (`site`) and
# applies it to every response. No build step is involved — it ships on push.
#
# Pages already sends `x-content-type-options: nosniff` and
# `referrer-policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin` by default; the additions
# here are CSP and HSTS.
#
# The CSP is strict because the site is nearly self-contained: fonts are
# self-hosted, images are local, and `theme.js` is the only script we author.
# If the site ever gains an inline `<script>`, an inline `style="…"` attribute,
# or another third-party embed, this breaks loudly — fix it with a nonce, not
# with 'unsafe-inline'.
#
#   script-src 'self'   — theme.js is a same-origin <script src>, no inline code.
#                         'none' would silently kill the light/dark toggle.
#   …cloudflareinsights — Cloudflare Web Analytics, injected at the edge and so
#                         absent from this repo. Deliberately kept on; without
#                         these two allowances the CSP blocks the beacon and the
#                         page-view counts silently stay empty. Drop both if
#                         analytics is ever switched off in the Pages settings.
#   img-src data:       — allows inline SVG/data URIs; no remote images are used.
#   frame-ancestors     — clickjacking; X-Frame-Options repeats it for old agents.
#   form-action 'none'  — the site has no forms, and should not grow one silently.
#
# HSTS carries no `preload` on purpose: preloading is effectively irreversible
# and should be a deliberate, separate decision.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src https://cloudflareinsights.com; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
